record legeos.papercut.lege-dev-deploy-restarts-lege-hostd-service-and/1 : papercut {
    title "`lege dev deploy` restarts lege-hostd.service and it crash-loops: zbus…"
    state verified
    statement """
        `lege dev deploy` restarts lege-hostd.service and it crash-loops: zbus fails "claiming org.legeos.Host on the system bus" with a raw EACCES connecting to /var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket (0666, root:root). Ruled out: AppArmor profile is confirmed complain-mode (would only log, not block); org.legeos.Host.conf is correctly shipped under /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/; a plain `sudo -u root` shell can read/write the socket fine. Unit has no explicit sandboxing beyond ProtectHome=yes/NoNewPrivileges=no; RestrictAddressFamilies/SystemCallFilter show unset. Root cause still unknown — worth a fresh look with strace on the actual ExecStart process. Not blocking desktop-session testing (hostd isn't in the login path); packages were already fully installed by the time this surfaced.
        """
    observed_at git:f5007ef369d0b386fb872a6b726e3f8baaac5944
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-01
}

record legeos.papercut.lege-dev-repo-verify-reports-a-blunt-verify/1 : papercut {
    title "`lege dev repo verify` reports a blunt \"verify: FAILED\" when the real…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        `lege dev repo verify` reports a blunt "verify: FAILED" when the real problem is that /var/lib/legeos/devrepo/gnupg is drwx------ root:root and the command runs as the user, so gpg cannot read the keyring at all ("unsafe ownership on homedir", "Permission denied", then "Can't check signature: No public key"). The archive itself verified fine — both sets reported "ok (13 pinned package(s))" — so the only thing that failed was a check that cannot succeed for this user by construction. It should say it cannot read the archive's keyring as this user, rather than reporting the signature as unverified, which reads like tampering.
        """
    observed_at git:d9ab0344cdb3af1778b584c03b0ccf8707452bb8
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-04
}

record legeos.papercut.lege-dev-repo-verify-reports-a-blunt-verify/2 : papercut {
    title "`lege dev repo verify` reports a blunt \"verify: FAILED\" when the real…"
    state verified
