record legeos.papercut.reading-templar-shell-lines-from-the-templaros/1 : papercut {
    title "Reading templar-shell lines from the TemplarOS journal (journalctl…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        Reading templar-shell lines from the TemplarOS journal (journalctl --directory on the mounted root): the shell writes ANSI-coloured tracing output, so journald stores every MESSAGE as a byte array and grep/jq see numbers, not text. Disabling ANSI when stdout is not a TTY (tracing_subscriber .with_ansi(false)) would make the journal searchable. Also: no icon-miss lines exist because they are debug-level.
        """
    observed_at git:2bc8f741f3c21759c3e7c728d9c211868035aa18
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-04
}

