    statement """
        scripts/nested-session.sh refuses to start whenever lege-comp.service/lege-sessiond.service are active, which is exactly the situation the lane rules said to validate compositor changes in — so the sanctioned validation path is unusable from inside a live LegeOS session. Starting lege-comp --backend winit plus lege-shell --surface by hand worked and claims no bus name; a `--no-daemons` mode (compositor + shell only, skipping the bus-claiming daemons and therefore the refusal) would make the documented path work.
        """
    observed_at git:ed81cb99ed494cf979d7435d6671596e1888a818
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-07
}

