record legeos.papercut.the-genuine-firmware-guest-candidate-boot/1 : papercut {
    title "The genuine firmware guest candidate boot exposed a real startup race:…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The genuine firmware guest candidate boot exposed a real startup race: hostd advertised org.templaros.Host before its object server existed, so the first Deployments1 call timed out despite subsequent readiness. Moved name acquisition after recovery and all registrations, using filed/sessiond convention; proving the first native API after ownership with a 1s deadline on a private bus.
        """
    observed_at git:7c68786687bea7b20dbc382bdacc2804e7284b70
    author "Main"
    created_at 2026-10-06
}

record legeos.papercut.the-guest-handoff-named-captured-guest-proof-sh/1 : papercut {
    title "The guest handoff named captured /guest-proof.sh but omitted its actual…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The guest handoff named captured /guest-proof.sh but omitted its actual assembly directory. The inferred root/guest-proof.sh was absent; an exact filename glob located the retained root-level driver before the independent firmware interrupted-stage proof.
        """
    observed_at git:7c68786687bea7b20dbc382bdacc2804e7284b70
    author "Main"
    created_at 2026-10-06
}

record legeos.papercut.the-home-field-s-own-reflow-focus-ops-tests-are/1 : papercut {
    title "The Home Field's own reflow/focus/ops tests are thorough, but nothing…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The Home Field's own reflow/focus/ops tests are thorough, but nothing in the shell exercises a widget's declared regions through a real Ui with input — the field_screen harness always passes an empty widget map. So the session tile's rung assignment and its click routing had no coverage at all, and the inverted rung rule (Shut down at the floor, Log out hidden) was invisible to the suite. Teaching the harness to carry WidgetSnapshots would let every widget's controls be tested where they are actually drawn.
        """
    observed_at git:1d8611042a47c81297b8a2a3db2a2ff977f8a8cc
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-26
}

record legeos.papercut.the-ignored-two-million-row-scale-test/1 : papercut {
    title "The ignored two-million-row scale test advertises about 1 GiB of…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The ignored two-million-row scale test advertises about 1 GiB of scratch, but its live tmpfs WAL reached 5.34 GiB and MemoryHigh throttled hundreds of thousands of times. Stopped only the attested owned test and removed its captured fixture after reaping; use disk-backed owned guest storage for the full scale journey.
        """
    observed_at git:12295f351ab14e649f900573190060cd88a7251e
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-10-08
}

record legeos.papercut.the-image-seeded-cosmic-term-while-the-terminal/1 : papercut {
    title "The image seeded cosmic-term while the Terminal provider role's default…"
    state superseded
    statement """
        The image seeded cosmic-term while the Terminal provider role's default is kitty (crates/lege-session-core/src/providers.rs:157) and legeos-shell ships /etc/xdg/kitty/kitty.conf as a deb asset — so the declared default terminal was not in any package list. Found while writing distro/seeds/selection.toml; fixed there by seeding kitty with the role and dropping cosmic-term. Two independent lists of package names is how this happens.
        """
    observed_at git:8b284c9147b70b4f03bb7c48ec993647e2e4df31
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-09-03
}

